The section must do:
- The seating chart: attendees sorted by seniority rank, lowest rank first, then placed seat by seat in the chosen fill order (front to back or back to front), seatsPerRow seats to a row, each seat labelled with the person's name and rank.
- Sorting and seat placement on the chart

The person sets these on the screen and nothing else uses them yet; the section uses them:
- "Fill order": state.seatOrderIndex (the index of the chosen option: Front to back, Back to front)

The program already has these: use them, do not make your own:
- a list of entries: state.entries is LogEntry[] with the fields {name: string, rank: number, minute: number}. Its form, its Add and Remove buttons and its rows are already on the screen. The section makes no list of its own for the same entries; to add one it copies state.entries into a new array, pushes a LogEntry (minute: time.hourOfDay() * 60 + time.minuteOfHour()) and returns {entries: thatArray __PASSTHROUGH__}.

